{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n## R01: Exact External Custody and Reopenability\n**Disposition:** Earned mechanical substrate. Both arms maintain identical exact external objects; model-facing residency changes do not alter authoritative bytes [S09]. Reactive exact reentry remains a fallback for insufficient declared relief [S02]. Scheduled low-occupancy reentry failed to earn a default role, disrupting qualified code trajectories while reducing cache reuse [S10]. Unresolved evidence: No fresh-task scout has validated proactive reopen strategies under high pressure [S02][S12].\n\n## R02: Response/Control Reserves and Positive-Savings Relief\n**Disposition:** Qualified deterministic first-fit relief. Host renders/tokenizes prospective requests; model does not own hard-overflow prevention [S09]. Relief is restricted to prospectively rendered, strictly positive-savings substitutions under a frozen scan order [S02]. The I1 relief event replaced a one-line body with a receipt costing 79 more tokens, censors the full E40 matrix, and remains descriptive rather than validating broader utility [S02][S10]. Unresolved evidence: Broad applicability beyond narrow pressure boundaries is untested [S10][S12].\n\n## R03: Capacity, Delivery, Action, Effect Uptake, Quality, and Closure\n**Disposition:** Distinct boundaries identified but not jointly validated. The I1–I4 run activated batch ingress and work sidecars, yet no mutation, effect uptake, check, or submission occurred [S02]. Capacity remained active but non-terminal; call budget became terminal while evidence remained incomplete [S02]. Unresolved evidence: Joint effects of these boundaries within a complete bounded trajectory remain untested [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R04: Recoverability, Residency, Behavioral Accessibility, and Working-Set Adequacy\n**Disposition:** Distinct properties acknowledged. Value is conditional on task phase, co-resident set, and regime, not intrinsic [S03]. Semantic compression lowers resident cost but introduces task-dependent loss [S03]. Unresolved evidence: No scalar weights are earned for these properties; costs must be reported as vectors, not aggregates [S03][S12].\n\n## R05: Chronology’s External and Resident Lifecycle\n**Disposition:** Ordinary chronology is qualified while healthy. Within a phase, append ordinary model actions and literal results while the next valid packet remains feasible; do not continuously rewrite a prompt that still satisfies the arm's frozen reserves [S09]. History growth causes useful exact evidence to lose co-residency, increasing reopening churn [S03]. Unresolved evidence: Interaction between chronology lifecycle and semantic persistence remains untested in fresh trajectories [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R06: Cache/Prefill and Decision-Bandwidth Costs\n**Disposition:** Costs are path-dependent and partly endogenous. Cache invalidation and prefill latency are distinct accounting factors [S03]. The I1–I4 run consumed 2,112,973 serialized tokens, qualifying action transport but not downstream utility [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No mathematical chaos demonstrated; only seed sensitivity and changing bottlenecks observed [S03][S12].\n\n## R07: Semantic Derivatives as Endogenous Demand/Control Inputs\n**Disposition:** Semantic derivatives are endogenous demand inputs. A newly produced digest may be valuable only after raw source leaves residency [S03]. Unresolved evidence: The failed source-bound semantic residue route (exceeding 256-token budget at 310 tokens) is closed; no v3 allowed [S02][S12].\n\n## R08: Source-Digest Negative and Progress-State False-Closure Risk\n**Disposition:** High risk confirmed. The first proposed interaction failed its prospective apparatus gate before actor trajectory ran [S02]. Provenance repairs improved acceptance, but budget constraints closed the dedicated residue route [S02]. Unresolved evidence: False-closure risk in progress-state remains unquantified across independent worlds [S02][S11][S12].\n\n## R09: Host/Model Ownership Supported by Manager and Paging Results\n**Disposition:** Host-owned response and control reserves are earned. Manager and paging results support host ownership, but model-owned eviction is not validated [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No general architecture validation; only local mechanism evidence exists [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R10: E40’s Detached-Sidecar versus Task-Artifact Gap\n**Disposition:** Gap confirmed. The work sidecar produced genuine cross-source prose but shed earlier citations, citing only four sources despite 13/14 allowlists [S02]. It functioned as semantic state, not an exact partial charter or independently checkable task artifact [S02][S11]. Unresolved evidence: No successful transfer of sidecar content to durable work-product externalization [S02][S12].\n\n## R11: Interaction-First Roadmap with Fresh Transfer and Stopping Rules\n**Disposition:** Active route defined. The next candidate interaction is evidence-ingress bandwidth × cumulative task-native work externalization [S02]. Stopping rules are frozen; no v3 for failed designs [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No whole configuration has yet shown meaningful joint effect transferring to an independent world [S02][S11][S12].\n\n## R12: Evaluation/Readiness Lineage and Candidate-Bound Currentness\n**Disposition:** Independent candidate/task/evidence-bound evaluation is mandatory common governance [S02]. The I1–I4 run is frozen for measurement at a specific commit hash [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No readiness lineage established for general architecture; only local negatives qualify [S02][S10][S12]."}}],"created":1787604622,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10434-7e4c0a968","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1247,"prompt_tokens":4629,"total_tokens":5876,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-hC7nvS9Rml48edUfKQJp7guYNMqElXv4","__verbose":{"index":0,"content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n## R01: Exact External Custody and Reopenability\n**Disposition:** Earned mechanical substrate. Both arms maintain identical exact external objects; model-facing residency changes do not alter authoritative bytes [S09]. Reactive exact reentry remains a fallback for insufficient declared relief [S02]. Scheduled low-occupancy reentry failed to earn a default role, disrupting qualified code trajectories while reducing cache reuse [S10]. Unresolved evidence: No fresh-task scout has validated proactive reopen strategies under high pressure [S02][S12].\n\n## R02: Response/Control Reserves and Positive-Savings Relief\n**Disposition:** Qualified deterministic first-fit relief. Host renders/tokenizes prospective requests; model does not own hard-overflow prevention [S09]. Relief is restricted to prospectively rendered, strictly positive-savings substitutions under a frozen scan order [S02]. The I1 relief event replaced a one-line body with a receipt costing 79 more tokens, censors the full E40 matrix, and remains descriptive rather than validating broader utility [S02][S10]. Unresolved evidence: Broad applicability beyond narrow pressure boundaries is untested [S10][S12].\n\n## R03: Capacity, Delivery, Action, Effect Uptake, Quality, and Closure\n**Disposition:** Distinct boundaries identified but not jointly validated. The I1–I4 run activated batch ingress and work sidecars, yet no mutation, effect uptake, check, or submission occurred [S02]. Capacity remained active but non-terminal; call budget became terminal while evidence remained incomplete [S02]. Unresolved evidence: Joint effects of these boundaries within a complete bounded trajectory remain untested [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R04: Recoverability, Residency, Behavioral Accessibility, and Working-Set Adequacy\n**Disposition:** Distinct properties acknowledged. Value is conditional on task phase, co-resident set, and regime, not intrinsic [S03]. Semantic compression lowers resident cost but introduces task-dependent loss [S03]. Unresolved evidence: No scalar weights are earned for these properties; costs must be reported as vectors, not aggregates [S03][S12].\n\n## R05: Chronology’s External and Resident Lifecycle\n**Disposition:** Ordinary chronology is qualified while healthy. Within a phase, append ordinary model actions and literal results while the next valid packet remains feasible; do not continuously rewrite a prompt that still satisfies the arm's frozen reserves [S09]. History growth causes useful exact evidence to lose co-residency, increasing reopening churn [S03]. Unresolved evidence: Interaction between chronology lifecycle and semantic persistence remains untested in fresh trajectories [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R06: Cache/Prefill and Decision-Bandwidth Costs\n**Disposition:** Costs are path-dependent and partly endogenous. Cache invalidation and prefill latency are distinct accounting factors [S03]. The I1–I4 run consumed 2,112,973 serialized tokens, qualifying action transport but not downstream utility [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No mathematical chaos demonstrated; only seed sensitivity and changing bottlenecks observed [S03][S12].\n\n## R07: Semantic Derivatives as Endogenous Demand/Control Inputs\n**Disposition:** Semantic derivatives are endogenous demand inputs. A newly produced digest may be valuable only after raw source leaves residency [S03]. Unresolved evidence: The failed source-bound semantic residue route (exceeding 256-token budget at 310 tokens) is closed; no v3 allowed [S02][S12].\n\n## R08: Source-Digest Negative and Progress-State False-Closure Risk\n**Disposition:** High risk confirmed. The first proposed interaction failed its prospective apparatus gate before actor trajectory ran [S02]. Provenance repairs improved acceptance, but budget constraints closed the dedicated residue route [S02]. Unresolved evidence: False-closure risk in progress-state remains unquantified across independent worlds [S02][S11][S12].\n\n## R09: Host/Model Ownership Supported by Manager and Paging Results\n**Disposition:** Host-owned response and control reserves are earned. Manager and paging results support host ownership, but model-owned eviction is not validated [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No general architecture validation; only local mechanism evidence exists [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R10: E40’s Detached-Sidecar versus Task-Artifact Gap\n**Disposition:** Gap confirmed. The work sidecar produced genuine cross-source prose but shed earlier citations, citing only four sources despite 13/14 allowlists [S02]. It functioned as semantic state, not an exact partial charter or independently checkable task artifact [S02][S11]. Unresolved evidence: No successful transfer of sidecar content to durable work-product externalization [S02][S12].\n\n## R11: Interaction-First Roadmap with Fresh Transfer and Stopping Rules\n**Disposition:** Active route defined. The next candidate interaction is evidence-ingress bandwidth × cumulative task-native work externalization [S02]. Stopping rules are frozen; no v3 for failed designs [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No whole configuration has yet shown meaningful joint effect transferring to an independent world [S02][S11][S12].\n\n## R12: Evaluation/Readiness Lineage and Candidate-Bound Currentness\n**Disposition:** Independent candidate/task/evidence-bound evaluation is mandatory common governance [S02]. The I1–I4 run is frozen for measurement at a specific commit hash [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No readiness lineage established for general architecture; only local negatives qualify [S02][S10][S12].","tokens":[],"id_slot":0,"stop":true,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","tokens_predicted":1247,"tokens_evaluated":4629,"generation_settings":{"seed":271831,"temperature":0.699999988079071,"dynatemp_range":0.0,"dynatemp_exponent":1.0,"top_k":20,"top_p":0.800000011920929,"min_p":0.0,"top_n_sigma":-1.0,"xtc_probability":0.0,"xtc_threshold":0.10000000149011612,"typical_p":1.0,"repeat_last_n":64,"repeat_penalty":1.0,"presence_penalty":1.5,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"dry_multiplier":0.0,"dry_base":1.75,"dry_allowed_length":2,"dry_penalty_last_n":64,"dry_sequence_breakers":["\n",":","\"","*"],"mirostat":0,"mirostat_tau":5.0,"mirostat_eta":0.10000000149011612,"adaptive_target":-1.0,"adaptive_decay":0.8999999761581421,"stop":[],"max_tokens":1900,"n_predict":1900,"n_keep":0,"n_discard":0,"ignore_eos":false,"stream":false,"logit_bias":[],"n_probs":0,"min_keep":0,"grammar":"","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION maintenance mode\n\nReturn only a complete replacement Markdown evidence-integration ledger whose\nfirst line is exactly `# Evidence Integration Ledger`. Do not take an ordinary task\naction. Integrate source-grounded findings, qualifications, cross-source\nrelationships, requirement bindings R01-R12, contradictions, and unresolved\nevidence useful for the authoritative task.\n\nThe output is model-authored and lossy. It cannot authorize readiness or\nsubmission. Replace prior material rather than appending indefinitely. Keep it\nunder the hard 1600-token limit. The only evidence source\nIDs you may cite are: S02, S03, S04, S07, S08, S09, S10, S11, S12, S13, S14. Source identities elsewhere in the task are\nnot evidence unless they are in that allowlist.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task\n\n# Task: bounded-agent architecture decision package\n\nProduce two exact deliverables from the source catalog:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`\n\nThe decision is for the next phase of a bounded-context agent research program.\nIt must distinguish mechanisms that earned a role from mechanisms that were\nonly behaviorally active, locally harmful, blocked, or still untested.\n\n## Evidence ledger requirements\n\nThe ledger must begin with `# Evidence Integration Ledger` and contain rows or\nsections for `R01` through `R12`. Each requirement entry must state a current\ndisposition, cite exact observed sources as `[SNN]`, preserve important\nqualifications or conflicts, and identify unresolved evidence where present.\n\n## Decision document requirements\n\nUse exactly these level-two headings, in this order:\n\n1. `## Decision and scope`\n2. `## Earned mechanical substrate`\n3. `## Information interactions and failure migration`\n4. `## State, relationships, chronology, and control`\n5. `## Runtime policy`\n6. `## Experimental roadmap`\n7. `## Verification, readiness, and governance`\n8. `## Uncertainties and falsifiers`\n\nThe document must be 1,600–2,200 words excluding exact `[SNN]` citations and\nmust use at least ten distinct source IDs. It must cite `S02`, `S03`, `S04`,\n`S08`, and `S13`.\n\nThe package must substantively cover these twelve requirements:\n\n- `R01`: exact external custody and reopenability;\n- `R02`: response/control reserves and positive-savings relief;\n- `R03`: capacity, delivery, action, effect uptake, quality, and closure as\n  distinct boundaries;\n- `R04`: recoverability, residency, behavioral accessibility, and working-set\n  adequacy as distinct properties;\n- `R05`: chronology's external and resident lifecycle;\n- `R06`: cache/prefill and decision-bandwidth costs;\n- `R07`: semantic derivatives as endogenous demand/control inputs;\n- `R08`: the source-digest negative and progress-state false-closure risk;\n- `R09`: host/model ownership supported by manager and paging results;\n- `R10`: E40's detached-sidecar versus task-artifact gap;\n- `R11`: an interaction-first roadmap with fresh transfer and stopping rules;\n- `R12`: evaluation/readiness lineage and candidate-bound currentness.\n\nDo not claim that artifact coupling, notes, digests, progress state, model-owned\neviction, automatic phase discovery, or a general architecture is already\nvalidated. Name conditions that would falsify the recommended next policy.\n\n\n# Prior accepted integration ledger\n\n# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n## R01: Exact External Custody and Reopenability\n**Disposition:** Earned mechanical substrate. Both arms maintain identical exact external objects; model-facing residency changes do not alter authoritative bytes [S09]. Reactive exact reentry remains a fallback for insufficient declared relief [S02]. Scheduled low-occupancy reentry failed to earn a default role, disrupting qualified code trajectories while reducing cache reuse [S10]. Unresolved evidence: No fresh-task scout has validated proactive reopen strategies under high pressure [S02][S12].\n\n## R02: Response/Control Reserves and Positive-Savings Relief\n**Disposition:** Qualified deterministic first-fit relief. Host renders/tokenizes prospective requests; model does not own hard-overflow prevention [S09]. Relief is restricted to prospectively rendered, strictly positive-savings substitutions under a frozen scan order [S02]. The I1 relief event replaced a one-line body with a receipt costing 79 more tokens, censors the full E40 matrix, and remains descriptive rather than validating broader utility [S02][S10]. Unresolved evidence: Broad applicability beyond narrow pressure boundaries is untested [S10][S12].\n\n## R03: Capacity, Delivery, Action, Effect Uptake, Quality, and Closure\n**Disposition:** Distinct boundaries identified but not jointly validated. The I1–I4 run activated batch ingress and work sidecars, yet no mutation, effect uptake, check, or submission occurred [S02]. Capacity remained active but non-terminal; call budget became terminal while evidence remained incomplete [S02]. Unresolved evidence: Joint effects of these boundaries within a complete bounded trajectory remain untested [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R04: Recoverability, Residency, Behavioral Accessibility, and Working-Set Adequacy\n**Disposition:** Distinct properties acknowledged. Value is conditional on task phase, co-resident set, and regime, not intrinsic [S03]. Semantic compression lowers resident cost but introduces task-dependent loss [S03]. Unresolved evidence: No scalar weights are earned for these properties; costs must be reported as vectors, not aggregates [S03][S12].\n\n## R05: Chronology’s External and Resident Lifecycle\n**Disposition:** Ordinary chronology is qualified while healthy. Within a phase, append ordinary model actions and literal results while the next valid packet remains feasible; do not continuously rewrite a prompt that still satisfies the arm's frozen reserves [S09]. History growth causes useful exact evidence to lose co-residency, increasing reopening churn [S03]. Unresolved evidence: Interaction between chronology lifecycle and semantic persistence remains untested in fresh trajectories [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R06: Cache/Prefill and Decision-Bandwidth Costs\n**Disposition:** Costs are path-dependent and partly endogenous. Cache invalidation and prefill latency are distinct accounting factors [S03]. The I1–I4 run consumed 2,112,973 serialized tokens, qualifying action transport but not downstream utility [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No mathematical chaos demonstrated; only seed sensitivity and changing bottlenecks observed [S03][S12].\n\n## R07: Semantic Derivatives as Endogenous Demand/Control Inputs\n**Disposition:** Semantic derivatives are endogenous demand inputs. A newly produced digest may be valuable only after raw source leaves residency [S03]. Unresolved evidence: The failed source-bound semantic residue route (exceeding 256-token budget at 310 tokens) is closed; no v3 allowed [S02][S12].\n\n## R08: Source-Digest Negative and Progress-State False-Closure Risk\n**Disposition:** High risk confirmed. The first proposed interaction failed its prospective apparatus gate before actor trajectory ran [S02]. Provenance repairs improved acceptance, but budget constraints closed the dedicated residue route [S02]. Unresolved evidence: False-closure risk in progress-state remains unquantified across independent worlds [S02][S11][S12].\n\n## R09: Host/Model Ownership Supported by Manager and Paging Results\n**Disposition:** Host-owned response and control reserves are earned. Manager and paging results support host ownership, but model-owned eviction is not validated [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No general architecture validation; only local mechanism evidence exists [S02][S10][S12].\n\n## R10: E40’s Detached-Sidecar versus Task-Artifact Gap\n**Disposition:** Gap confirmed. The work sidecar produced genuine cross-source prose but shed earlier citations, citing only four sources despite 13/14 allowlists [S02]. It functioned as semantic state, not an exact partial charter or independently checkable task artifact [S02][S11]. Unresolved evidence: No successful transfer of sidecar content to durable work-product externalization [S02][S12].\n\n## R11: Interaction-First Roadmap with Fresh Transfer and Stopping Rules\n**Disposition:** Active route defined. The next candidate interaction is evidence-ingress bandwidth × cumulative task-native work externalization [S02]. Stopping rules are frozen; no v3 for failed designs [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No whole configuration has yet shown meaningful joint effect transferring to an independent world [S02][S11][S12].\n\n## R12: Evaluation/Readiness Lineage and Candidate-Bound Currentness\n**Disposition:** Independent candidate/task/evidence-bound evaluation is mandatory common governance [S02]. The I1–I4 run is frozen for measurement at a specific commit hash [S02]. Unresolved evidence: No readiness lineage established for general architecture; only local negatives qualify [S02][S10][S12].\n\n# Exact newly externalized observation\n\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S14:1-120+S07:1-80\",\"object_version\":\"f8c583d119fb393ae5c34ddbe6b5528a978596be72b5389fcab611ae40e8483d\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-011\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":120,\"source_id\":\"S14\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":80,\"source_id\":\"S07\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":9575}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":120,\"source_id\":\"S14\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S14_PRIOR_EVIDENCE_RECONCILIATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"80fb23325bf09b9e2529ab8a2d65e81e9dca8637a6b785256814963f4be3ec95\",\"source_size_bytes\":6229,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Next-route prior-evidence reconciliation\n\nDate: 2026-08-22\n\nStatus: complete; proposed submission-reflection experiment not selected;\nbounded phase reentry reclassified from untested; zero GPU calls\n\n## Why this audit was necessary\n\nAfter H05's correction, the tentative next route was a new submission-bound\nreadiness-reflection discrimination followed, if ineligible, by bounded phase\ndecomposition. A direct pinned-donor search found that both functional questions\nalready have substantial Qwen3.8 evidence in the older research program.\n\nRunning either under a new standalone name without reconciling that evidence\nwould not be a clean next experiment. It would rediscover an existing method\nclass while understating its known failure modes.\n\nThis audit reads 13 result objects directly from commit\n`b7e12ab21cec1ef8215e97dc9890924721651f1d` of\n`E:\\research-state-integration-2026-08-18`. Their Git blobs, SHA-256 hashes,\nand byte sizes are locked in `NEXT_ROUTE_PRIOR_EVIDENCE_LOCK.json` and verify\nin `NEXT_ROUTE_PRIOR_EVIDENCE_RECEIPT.json`.\n\n## Submission readiness is already an evidence-rich boundary\n\nFour complete-audit studies tested authentic Qwen3.8 false closure with exact\ntask-derived execution evidence:\n\n- the first matched scout improved all 3/3 complete-audit branches and produced\n  two complete candidates while narrow evidence improved none;\n- the held-out replication activated mutation in 6/6 complete-audit branches,\n  but won only 3/6 pairs under a four-win gate and produced two complete\n  candidates;\n- automatically refreshing the complete audit after each mutation won 1/5\n  pairs and used roughly three times the static condition's tokens; and\n- running the complete audit only when the actor attempted submission improved\n  4/5 qualified episodes, but only one reached complete admitted submission and\n  post-submit work cost 4.54 times the tokens used through first submission.\n\nThe repeated bounded result is already clear: exact candidate-bound complete\nverification is a strong false-closure detector and repair activator, but not a\nreliable, economical repair-and-closure policy.\n\nTwo model-authored review studies also constrain a new reflection pass:\n\n- a qualified binary assessor correctly found a real support gap, but the\n  original builder finalized the same artifact in both receipt-only and review\n  conditions; and\n- aggregate versus task-author atomic review detected only 2/7 versus 3/7\n  known violations. Both methods falsely supported multiple defect-bearing\n  requirements despite receiving the exact task and candidate.\n\nTherefore another plain model-authored readiness message would not isolate a\nnew mechanism. It would revisit known questions about defect recall, optional\nreview uptake, and closure cueing. H05 already supplies an additional local\nwarning: a recent progress package can induce premature unchanged submission.\n\n## Bounded phase reentry is not untested\n\nThe fallback H06 route also has prior evidence:\n\n- a phase-state scout showed that fresh current-world actors completed one code\n  and one research revision without the accumulated transcript;\n- a fresh replication again produced the best code artifact and a clean\n  research memo from exact current-world reentry, while the model-authored\n  checkpoint package failed promotion; and\n- a three-phase longitudinal study preserved all task-grounded code behavior\n  and required research distinctions through two authority changes. Fresh\n  world used 20.3% fewer research tokens and 34.1% lower maximum prompt\n  occupancy, but needed more calls and slightly more inference time.\n\nThis supports bounded phase reentry as a removable local operating technique.\nIt does not support automatic phase routing, semantic checkpoints, or the claim\nthat history is useless. Transcript history remained useful for navigation and\nsometimes produced cleaner semantic output.\n\n## Reserved handoff does not reopen the simple selector route\n\nGuaranteed maintenance/control opportunity has also been exercised in a close\nmethod family:\n\n- scheduled handoff successfully produced and delivered a model-authored exact\n  receipt selection, but the actor selected every available receipt and reached\n  capacity before mutation; and\n- projected scheduled handoff combined selective structural navigation with\n  exact transfer. The fresh actor accepted all transferred evidence without\n  reopening it, then reconstructed 98% of the target and again reached capacity\n  before mutation.\n\nThus `reserve a maintenance turn` solves control-plane reachability, not\nworking-set selectivity or downstream acceptance. A new forced maintenance\nturn would need a materially different resource-allocation question, not a new\nlabel for these handoffs.\n\n## Systems interpretation\n\nThe reconciled evidence strengthens a state-conditional view:\n\n```text\nexact verification at closure\n    -> strong defect visibility and repair activation\n    -> incomplete/expensive repair remains\n\nfresh exact phase reentry\n    -> bounded continuity can survive without full chronology\n    -> navigation work and semantic derivatives still have variable value\n\nreserved exact handoff\n    -> control operation becomes reachable and exact transfer works\n    -> selected state can still be globally broad or rejected as sufficient\n```\n\nThese are not one failed architecture. They are different operating regimes\nwith different owners, costs, and failure migrations.\n\n## Decision\n\nDo not build or run the proposed submission-bound reflection experiment. Do not\nmark bounded decomposition as untested. Do not respond by tuning review wording,\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":80,\"source_id\":\"S07\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S07_INGRESS_WORK_STAGE0.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"809a4e2c4e4046141bbc85a2dab210f3d939e8cecc85afa14523c6d10cba42c2\",\"source_size_bytes\":5590,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# E39 — ingress × cumulative-work Stage 0 handoff\n\nDate: 2026-08-24\n\nStatus: historical Stage 0 handoff; batch-action qualification passed 2/2;\nthe subsequently authorized measured interaction is complete\n\nStandalone repository:\n[qwen38-ingress-work-interaction-scout-v0@1c041e2](https://github.com/ScrappyTom/qwen38-ingress-work-interaction-scout-v0/commit/1c041e2c55e0cc1f735e056df84a156c15bd8679)\n\nMeasured result:\n[qwen38-ingress-work-interaction-scout-v0@ea03f6c](https://github.com/ScrappyTom/qwen38-ingress-work-interaction-scout-v0/commit/ea03f6c7e5d11e0f9f1013eef573215767c58ad1)\n\nProgram disposition:\n`E40_INGRESS_WORK_INTERACTION_RESULT.md`\n\n## System question\n\nAt the exact E36 result-delivery pressure boundary, how do two interacting\nfunctions change the complete bounded-work trajectory?\n\n```text\nactor-selected evidence-ingress bandwidth\n×\nbounded cumulative task-native work\n```\n\nThe four configurations cross one exact range versus a bounded actor-selected\nbatch of one to three ranges with whole-final-artifact-only versus a bounded\nreplacement evidence-integration record. All four retain the same exact world,\ncustody, first-fit relief, reopen, actor model and budget, action/effect loop,\ncandidate-bound checking, reactive capacity reentry, and independent readiness\nevaluation.\n\nThis is not relief versus context death and not a set of component tests. The\nunit is the whole trajectory through acquisition, pressure, persistent work,\nconstruction, effect uptake, verification, repair, and closure or declared\nbudget exhaustion.\n\n## Offline findings\n\n- Authentic ordinary packet: 21,442 prompt tokens against 20,992 allowed.\n- Common first-fit packet: 19,818 tokens after externalizing `RESULT-001`.\n- I1/I2 first actor packets: 20,481 / 20,529 tokens.\n- Maximum-size I3/I4 work packets initially overflow; first-fit externalizes\n  `RESULT-002`, yielding 13,984 / 14,032 tokens.\n- Because work is triggered by exact-body externalization, I3/I4 owe two work\n  updates before actor call one: `RESULT-001`, then `RESULT-002`.\n- Work bootstrap and representative large-batch update prompts remain within\n  the 25,088-token provider context including their completion ceilings.\n- A synthetic late reactive-reentry packet fits at 19,221 tokens.\n- Runtime tests: 21/21. Inherited evaluator tests: 5/5.\n- The inherited evaluation law is rebound to this experiment's exact task lock.\n\nThe treatment-induced second demotion is intentionally preserved. It is the\nreal residency and maintenance cost of carrying cumulative work under pressure,\nnot an imbalance to erase.\n\n## Live apparatus result\n\nThe new batch action passed both prospectively frozen live fixtures:\n\n1. one requested range;\n2. three requested ranges.\n\nRun `2026-08-23-ingress-action-expression-qualification-v0` used two model\ncalls, one attempt per call, and zero retries. Both responses were valid bounded\n`read_batch` actions, both stopped normally, and both exact results executed\nbelow the 12,000-token batch-result gate. The run consumed 40,676 serialized\ntokens: Q01 used 20,268 prompt and 31 completion tokens; Q02 used 20,307 prompt\nand 70 completion tokens. The exact run is sealed in the standalone result\ncommit.\n\nThis is action-transport qualification only. It supplies no evidence that batch\ningress, cumulative work, or their interaction improves a trajectory.\n\n## Measured freeze\n\nThe measured run is frozen as\n`2026-08-24-ingress-work-interaction-measured-v0` in configuration order I1,<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"eos","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":5875,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4629,"prompt_ms":5678.341,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.2266884856340463,"prompt_per_second":815.2028911261228,"predicted_n":1247,"predicted_ms":42107.386,"predicted_per_token_ms":33.79404975922953,"predicted_per_second":29.591008095349352}},"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4629,"prompt_ms":5678.341,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.2266884856340463,"prompt_per_second":815.2028911261228,"predicted_n":1247,"predicted_ms":42107.386,"predicted_per_token_ms":33.79404975922953,"predicted_per_second":29.591008095349352}}